      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix shared handler reference ownership in CPU KV offload.\n\nBefore this change, the store and load handlers received the same mutable\n`cpu_tensors` list. When one handler cleared its tensor references during\nshutdown, it also cleared the other handler's list. Each handler now owns its\nown reference container; the tensor objects and backing storage are not copied.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Give each `SingleDirectionOffloadingHandler` its own tensor-reference lists.\n- Preserve the existing shutdown and shared-region cleanup behavior.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- The targeted pytest suite was not rerun locally after this scope reduction.\n\nNo model evaluation is required because this change does not affect model\noutputs, accuracy, or serving behavior.\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare this change. The human submitter must review\nevery changed line and be able to explain the ownership and shutdown semantics\nbefore submission.",
