            },
            "body": "> Hey @Alex-ai-future,\r\n> \r\n> I understand why each handler needs its own tensor-reference list.\r\n> \r\n> For the additional private-buffer retention and device-wide synchronization, can you share a concrete failure scenario or reproducer? When would event synchronization fail while a transfer could still access the CPU buffers?\r\n> \r\n> We care about shutdown latency, so I’d like to understand what the extra synchronization protects against. In particular, if both synchronization attempts fail, is there a realistic case where transfers remain active rather than the worker needing to exit?\r\n\r\n\r\nI have also confirmed that this is a terminal shutdown path. I have removed the \"private-buffer,\" and since file path in the \"share region\" have been safely unlink (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/53073 can do it further). I believe that the failure handling about `torch.accelerator.synchronize() ` during the previous \"share region\" shutdown can also be eliminated. It seems that there are no negative side effects in practical use.\r\n\r\nI also want to thank you for taking the time to give me your advice.",
